Initial release — the borrower record

Borrowers, with guarantor and documents carried as JSON-shaped text.

A blank stored name is rendered as a placeholder and never written back as
one. `first_name` is NOT NULL but a handset can store an empty one, so the
repository substitutes something readable to keep list pages working — and an
earlier version then saved that substitute on any unrelated edit, renaming a
real person with nothing left to recover what they were called.

The JSON columns are deliberately permissive text rather than a `json` type.
They carry what v1 and the Firestore import hand over, some of which does not
parse, and the suite pins the behaviour: keep the unreadable blob, show what
can be shown, never silently discard it.
